why: `fresh[Db]` where a `module[Db]` installed the singleton is the
  mistake this vocabulary invites, and the compiler answers "No given
  instance of type okay.New[Db] ... for parameter n of method fresh",
  which names the type and not the fix.

what: `New` gains an @implicitNotFound saying both roads (wire the one
  the region installed, or have the PROVIDER offer a prototype), and
  `fresh` is respelled `New[A] ?=> (A ! Resource) = wire[New[A]]()` —
  which is what carries the message to the call site (measured: as a
  `using` parameter dotty prints its own text instead) and says in
  the code that fresh IS wire at another type.

next: apply, assert the message in a test, docs line
